Basic relationship:
$math{lim{x->a, f(x)} = L}
For any $math{\e > 0}, there exist $math{\d > 0} such that $math{|x-a|<\d => |f(x)-L|<\e}

$math{lim{x->\inf, f(x)} = L}
For any $math{\e > 0}, there exist $math{R > 0} such that $math{x>R => |f(x)-L|<\e}

Left limits (Vänstergränsvärde), Right limits (Högergränsvärde)

$math{lim{x->a, f(x)} = L}
f(x) does not have to be defined at $math{x=a}
When limit x approaches a, f(x) approaches L

Presetted values:
$math{lim{x->\inf, (ln(x))^300/x} = [t=ln(x)] = lim{t->\inf, t^300/e^t}}
$math{lim{x->\inf, ln(sqrt(x))/x} = [t=sqrt(x)] = lim{t->\inf, ln(x)/x^2}}
$math{lim{x->\inf, 2^ln(x)/x^ln(2)} = [t=ln(x)] = lim{t->\inf, 2^t/(e^t)^ln(2)}}

$math{lim{x->0, sin(x)/sin(3x)} = lim{x->0, (sin(x)/x)/(sin(3x)/x)}}
$math{lim{x->\inf, (x+cos(3x))/(2x+sin(x))} = lim{x->\inf, x(1+cos(3x)/x)/(x(2+sin(x)/x))}}
$math{lim{x->0, (e^(3x)-1)/(e^(4x)-1)} = lim{x->0, ((e^(3x)-1)/x)/((e^(4x)-1)/x)}}
$math{lim{x->0, xln(sin(x))} = lim{x->0, x(ln(x)+ln(sin(x)/x))}}

Basic relationship:
Vertical/Vertikal: $math{lim{x->0, f(x)}=\m\inf}
Horizontal/Horizontell: $math{lim{x->\inf, f(x)}=m}
Oblique/Sneda: $math{y=kx+m} $math{k=lim{x->\inf, f(x)/x}}, $math{m=lim{x->\inf, f(x)-kx}}
